title: SOFT and TEXT - Adjuvant endocrine therapy
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

* ''Takeaway:'' In premenopausal hormone receptor-positive early breast cancer, ovarian function suppression (OFS) offers greatest absolute benefit at higher recurrence risk; exemestane + OFS provides the greatest recurrence reduction. Tamoxifen alone remains reasonable for low-risk disease.
* ''SOFT — does OFS help?'' 3,066 women randomized to five years of tamoxifen, tamoxifen + OFS, or exemestane + OFS. Patients receiving chemotherapy had to remain premenopausal afterward. Fifteen-year breast cancer–free interval: 72.1%, 75.7%, and 78.6%, respectively; neither OFS regimen significantly improved overall survival across the entire trial population.
* ''TEXT — which endocrine partner?'' 2,672 women randomized to five years of exemestane + OFS versus tamoxifen + OFS. OFS began upfront, concurrently with chemotherapy when given. In the ''combined TEXT/SOFT analysis'', 15-year disease-free survival was 74.9% versus 71.3% (hazard ratio 0.82), favoring exemestane.
* ''Board pearl:'' Aromatase inhibitors require OFS in premenopausal patients. Balance recurrence reduction against menopausal symptoms, bone loss, and sexual dysfunction. These trials do not establish that OFS replaces [[chemotherapy|Adjuvant chemotherapy in HR-positive breast cancer - TAILORx to RxPONDER to OFSET]].

Sources: [[Trial design 2013|https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3855346/]]; [[Final outcomes 2026|https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13484932/]]; ASCO-SEP 2026, Breast Cancer, p. 462; NCCN Breast Cancer v6.2026 (July 29), BINV-K 3/4; Discussion MS-36–37.
